  "core_idea": "**Most** as an adverb means to the greatest degree; it can also mean *very* in formal use and *almost* in informal use.",
  "senses": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "signpost": "adjectives and adverbs",
      "definition": "used before an adjective or an adverb to say that something has a quality to a greater degree than all the others",
      "explanation": "Before an adjective it is usually used with **the**: *the most beautiful*. Use it with most adjectives of two or more syllables and with most adverbs that end in **-ly**; most one-syllable adjectives add **-est** instead: **biggest**, **fastest**.",
      "grammar": {
        "countability": null,
